{"artifacts":{"architecture-governor.json":{"sha256":"902fbf9c6cc390bd62d00d187ba9f97ffde13eb72613d1b0cf2d54c80a654404","text":"{\"context_sha256\":\"9a98df9989f7f67def256d38c2ec4af494278d7d9e6c51893bcfd2fa235b4dde\",\"contract_sha256\":\"f62a2becb08d5c4b757f50c5300450f609b15f59e46dfd79cc3eb76e280622ee\",\"convergence\":\"improves\",\"debts\":[\"DEBT-CHAT-AREA\",\"DEBT-SIDEBAR\"],\"decision\":\"proceed\",\"design_sha256\":\"bcf73d4f40a6a1c645ece2c4d13a41eeb9025380f38fa00eed2b940573f2a98b\",\"migrations\":[\"MIG-FRONTEND-LARGE-COMPONENTS\"],\"policy_sha256\":\"0db30c9f1e05383df234c84feb31dcef348f09ec605db423606b9f72c7e54add\",\"principles\":[\"ARCH-DEEP-MODULES\",\"ARCH-FRONTEND-BOUNDARIES\"],\"rationale\":[\"All seven ACs map to the named seam app/frontend/src/lib/exportMarkdown.ts#formatCitation, which the existing suite already exercises through the public interface, so the acceptance tests prove behaviour through the seam rather than internals.\",\"The repair stays inside the established deep module: three fallback return statements adopt the shape the valid paths already emit, adding no new export, parameter, helper, or configuration knob, so the module's interface neither widens nor forks.\",\"The change strengthens the seam's contract rather than expanding it: after the repair every non-blank-snippet entry starts with '- ' and carries the two-space-indented blockquote, so formatSources needs no knowledge of URL validity and the exported list can no longer silently merge items.\",\"Layer direction is respected: exportMarkdown.ts sits in frontend-lib (allowed_imports []), the design adds no imports and no dependency edge, and pure formatting stays in lib exactly as ARCH-FRONTEND-BOUNDARIES requires.\",\"No parallel abstraction is added beside an established seam (ARCH-DEEP-MODULES): the design reuses formatCitation and formatTimestamp, allowed_new_files is empty, and planned_files is exactly the one production file the issue names.\",\"DEBT-CHAT-AREA, DEBT-SIDEBAR, and MIG-FRONTEND-LARGE-COMPONENTS apply only through the context's derived impact set (ChatArea.tsx, Sidebar.tsx); planned_files touches neither file, so no no-growth hotspot grows and the migration's direction of keeping export behavior out of the large components is reinforced.\",\"Checked against the existing suite (exportMarkdown.test.ts:215-272): current fallback cases assert toContain on fragments that stay true of the repaired strings and pin no buggy exact shape, so nothing needs weakening, skipping, or removing, and the red proof correctly comes from new AC-1..AC-3 checkpoints asserting on result content so vitest displays the '(timestamp link unavailable) — 0:10–0:20' symptom.\",\"The planned repaired shapes in data_flows satisfy every contract invariant: '- ' marker on all entries, no '](' link in either fallback, the '\\\\n  > \\\"<snippet>\\\"' blockquote on its own line, the verbatim console.warn on both YouTube branches, and the untouched empty-snippet early guard (AC-7).\",\"Over a multi-ticket horizon the uniform entry shape gives future citation source types one established shape to conform to and lets the suite pin the whole formatCitation contract through the interface; the design creates no coupling, hotspot growth, or migration debt.\"],\"required_changes\":[],\"source_files\":[\"app/frontend/src/App.tsx\",\"app/frontend/src/__tests__/ChatArea-handleCitationClick.test.tsx\",\"app/frontend/src/__tests__/ChatArea-refreshConversationsRef.test.tsx\",\"app/frontend/src/__tests__/ChatArea-strictmode-first-send.test.tsx\",\"app/frontend/src/__tests__/VideoExplorer-admin-gate.test.tsx\",\"app/frontend/src/__tests__/VideoExplorer.test.tsx\",\"app/frontend/src/__tests__/adminApi.test.ts\",\"app/frontend/src/components/ChatArea.tsx\",\"app/frontend/src/components/CitationModal.test.tsx\",\"app/frontend/src/components/CitationModal.tsx\",\"app/frontend/src/components/Message.test.tsx\",\"app/frontend/src/components/Message.tsx\",\"app/frontend/src/components/Sidebar.test.tsx\",\"app/frontend/src/components/Sidebar.tsx\",\"app/frontend/src/components/VideoExplorer.tsx\",\"app/frontend/src/hooks/useAdminVideos.test.ts\",\"app/frontend/src/hooks/useAdminVideos.ts\",\"app/frontend/src/hooks/useConversations.test.ts\",\"app/frontend/src/hooks/useConversations.ts\",\"app/frontend/src/hooks/useMessages.ts\",\"app/frontend/src/hooks/useStreamingResponse.ts\",\"app/frontend/src/lib/api.ts\",\"app/frontend/src/lib/exportMarkdown.test.ts\",\"app/frontend/src/lib/exportMarkdown.ts\",\"app/frontend/src/pages/AdminVideos.tsx\"],\"version\":\"1.0\"}\n"},"architecture-governor.raw.json":{"sha256":"bb47d97b9404632cc1abe65d3a334289790d2b494809d3e2eec206e073f0b3e6","text":"{\n  \"version\": \"1.0\",\n  \"decision\": \"proceed\",\n  \"convergence\": \"improves\",\n  \"principles\": [\n    \"ARCH-DEEP-MODULES\",\n    \"ARCH-FRONTEND-BOUNDARIES\"\n  ],\n  \"migrations\": [\n    \"MIG-FRONTEND-LARGE-COMPONENTS\"\n  ],\n  \"debts\": [\n    \"DEBT-CHAT-AREA\",\n    \"DEBT-SIDEBAR\"\n  ],\n  \"rationale\": [\n    \"All seven ACs map to the named seam app/frontend/src/lib/exportMarkdown.ts#formatCitation, which the existing suite already exercises through the public interface, so the acceptance tests prove behaviour through the seam rather than internals.\",\n    \"The repair stays inside the established deep module: three fallback return statements adopt the shape the valid paths already emit, adding no new export, parameter, helper, or configuration knob, so the module's interface neither widens nor forks.\",\n    \"The change strengthens the seam's contract rather than expanding it: after the repair every non-blank-snippet entry starts with '- ' and carries the two-space-indented blockquote, so formatSources needs no knowledge of URL validity and the exported list can no longer silently merge items.\",\n    \"Layer direction is respected: exportMarkdown.ts sits in frontend-lib (allowed_imports []), the design adds no imports and no dependency edge, and pure formatting stays in lib exactly as ARCH-FRONTEND-BOUNDARIES requires.\",\n    \"No parallel abstraction is added beside an established seam (ARCH-DEEP-MODULES): the design reuses formatCitation and formatTimestamp, allowed_new_files is empty, and planned_files is exactly the one production file the issue names.\",\n    \"DEBT-CHAT-AREA, DEBT-SIDEBAR, and MIG-FRONTEND-LARGE-COMPONENTS apply only through the context's derived impact set (ChatArea.tsx, Sidebar.tsx); planned_files touches neither file, so no no-growth hotspot grows and the migration's direction of keeping export behavior out of the large components is reinforced.\",\n    \"Checked against the existing suite (exportMarkdown.test.ts:215-272): current fallback cases assert toContain on fragments that stay true of the repaired strings and pin no buggy exact shape, so nothing needs weakening, skipping, or removing, and the red proof correctly comes from new AC-1..AC-3 checkpoints asserting on result content so vitest displays the '(timestamp link unavailable) — 0:10–0:20' symptom.\",\n    \"The planned repaired shapes in data_flows satisfy every contract invariant: '- ' marker on all entries, no '](' link in either fallback, the '\\\\n  > \\\"<snippet>\\\"' blockquote on its own line, the verbatim console.warn on both YouTube branches, and the untouched empty-snippet early guard (AC-7).\",\n    \"Over a multi-ticket horizon the uniform entry shape gives future citation source types one established shape to conform to and lets the suite pin the whole formatCitation contract through the interface; the design creates no coupling, hotspot growth, or migration debt.\"\n  ],\n  \"required_changes\": [],\n  \"notes\": \"Copied the kernel-computed policy sets verbatim: DEBT-CHAT-AREA and DEBT-SIDEBAR arise solely because ChatArea.tsx/Sidebar.tsx appear in context.json's files (derived impact), not because the design touches them; the same holds for the single migration. Judgement call recorded: convergence is 'improves' rather than 'neutral' because the repair removes a real shape divergence among formatCitation's branches — before it, exported list items merged into the previous item depending on URL validity, an interface-level inconsistency; after it the module guarantees one uniform entry shape for every non-blank snippet, testable through the interface alone. Not a structural demand, advisory only: design.json's planned_files lists only the production file (correct under the plan-exact-production-files rule), while the contract's own invariants and the issue's expected-files section already name the existing exportMarkdown.test.ts as the confined location for the AC-1..AC-3 cases, so the test-file edit is contract-mandated and needs no entry in planned_files or required_changes. Residual risks the implementation must honour (already in the contract's risk list, restated for the coder): assert on result string content in red checkpoints so the symptom is visible; keep em dash (—) before ranges and en dash (–) inside ranges exactly as the existing source; mock console.warn with the existing vi.spyOn pattern in the new cases. No prefactor or decompose: the change is three return statements in an 87-line pure module with an established, already-tested seam.\"\n}\n"},"context.enriched.json":{"sha256":"beddff0a3bfc4c3b389846db25fafc6e8b7b55005b2e76a70b433003ac484adf","text":"{\"adrs\":[],\"callers\":[\"app/frontend/src/lib/exportMarkdown.ts#formatSources\",\"app/frontend/src/lib/exportMarkdown.ts#exportConversationAsMarkdown\",\"app/frontend/src/components/ChatArea.tsx#exportConversationAsMarkdown\",\"[derived] app/frontend/src/App.tsx\",\"[derived] app/frontend/src/components/ChatArea.tsx\",\"[derived] app/frontend/src/components/CitationModal.tsx\",\"[derived] app/frontend/src/components/Message.tsx\",\"[derived] app/frontend/src/components/Sidebar.tsx\",\"[derived] app/frontend/src/components/VideoExplorer.tsx\",\"[derived] app/frontend/src/hooks/useAdm