kdown.ts:63) joins formatCitation outputs with '\\\\n', which is exactly why a missing '- ' marker merges an entry into the previous list item. Callers: exportConversationAsMarkdown (same module, :74) is called from ChatArea.tsx:616 (the browser export button); ChatArea.tsx is out of scope to change. The Citation type (api.ts:46) declares snippet, source_type ('youtube' | 'dynamous' | string) and lesson_url as optional, which is why the empty/missing guards exist. Existing tests already pin: the empty/whitespace/missing snippet early guard returning '' (test :202-206), the verbatim console.warn on invalid video_url (test :215-227), the valid-URL happy path (:208-213), the valid Dynamous lesson_url path (:243-258), and both fallback shapes against the BUGGY strings (:215-227, :229-235, :260-272) — those three fallback tests assert substrings that stay true after repair ('Test Video Title', 'not [Test Video Title](', '(timestamp link unavailable)', '0:10–0:20', '> \\\"Test snippet text\\\"', 'no ](') so they keep passing unmodified; the new AC-1..AC-3 cases add the missing '- ' marker and blockquote assertions that go red today. No ADR directory exists (docs/adr/ absent; DECISION_REGISTER.md has no export/citation entries). Gotchas from the contract's risk list: en dash (–, U+2013) separates the timestamp range while em dash (—, U+2014) precedes it; the new red assertions must inspect the returned string's content (not boolean startsWith) so vitest prints the '(timestamp link unavailable) — 0:10–0:20' symptom; console.warn must be suppressed in the new fallback tests via the existing vi.spyOn(console, 'warn') pattern.\"\n}\n"},"design.json":{"sha256":"bcf73d4f40a6a1c645ece2c4d13a41eeb9025380f38fa00eed2b940573f2a98b","text":"{\"ac_mapping\":{\"AC-1\":[\"app/frontend/src/lib/exportMarkdown.ts#formatCitation\"],\"AC-2\":[\"app/frontend/src/lib/exportMarkdown.ts#formatCitation\"],\"AC-3\":[\"app/frontend/src/lib/exportMarkdown.ts#formatCitation\"],\"AC-4\":[\"app/frontend