id video_url: \\\"<url>\\\"' is emitted unchanged on both YouTube fallback branches (pinned verbatim by an existing test).\",\n    \"Only one production file changes: app/frontend/src/lib/exportMarkdown.ts; test changes are confined to app/frontend/src/lib/exportMarkdown.test.ts.\",\n    \"The empty/whitespace/missing-snippet early guard (exportMarkdown.ts:22) keeps returning '' before any URL handling — no marker, no blockquote, no console.warn (AC-7).\"\n  ],\n  \"data_flows\": [\n    \"Citation -> formatCitation -> markdown list entry string; happy paths: '- [title](url) — <range>\\\\n  > \\\"<snippet>\\\"'; repaired fallbacks: '- <title> (timestamp link unavailable) — <range>\\\\n  > \\\"<snippet>\\\"' (YouTube catch and no-v branches) and '- <title> — <range>\\\\n  > \\\"<snippet>\\\"' (Dynamous empty lesson_url)\",\n    \"formatCitation entries -> formatSources -> '\\\\n\\\\n**Sources:**\\\\n' + entries joined by '\\\\n' (single markdown list)\",\n    \"messages -> exportConversationAsMarkdown -> Blob via saveAs -> conversation-<slug>-<date>.md download\"\n  ],\n  \"ac_mapping\": {\n    \"AC-1\": [\"app/frontend/src/lib/exportMarkdown.ts#formatCitation\"],\n    \"AC-2\": [\"app/frontend/src/lib/exportMarkdown.ts#formatCitation\"],\n    \"AC-3\": [\"app/frontend/src/lib/exportMarkdown.ts#formatCitation\"],\n    \"AC-4\": [\"app/frontend/src/lib/exportMarkdown.ts#formatCitation\"],\n    \"AC-5\": [\"app/frontend/src/lib/exportMarkdown.ts#formatCitation\"],\n    \"AC-6\": [\"app/frontend/src/lib/exportMarkdown.ts#formatCitation\"],\n    \"AC-7\": [\"app/frontend/src/lib/exportMarkdown.ts#formatCitation\"]\n  },\n  \"planned_files\": [\n    \"app/frontend/src/lib/exportMarkdown.ts\"\n  ],\n  \"allowed_new_files\": [],\n  \"notes\": \"Smallest deep-module design: formatCitation is already the deep seam (every rendering rule lives behind one string-returning function, testable through its return value alone), so the repair is purely internal — conform the three fallback return statements (exportMarkdown.ts:32, :46, :53) to the shape lines :35 and :58 already emit: prepend the '- ' list marker and append '\\\\n  > \\\"<citation.snippet>\\\"'. Nothing is deleted (all existing returns are consumed by the same callers), no helper is added (rung 6 of the ladder: each repaired return is one direct template string), no new dependency, no new file. No dependencies declared in the contract, so no manifest/lockfile in planned_files. planned_files holds only the production file; the contract's invariants authorize test changes confined to app/frontend/src/lib/exportMarkdown.test.ts (listed in context.tests), where AC-1..AC-3 acceptance cases are appended as new `it` blocks in the existing formatCitation describe using the suite's baseCitation spread — new assertions must inspect the returned string's content (toMatch on the result) so the red run prints the '(timestamp link unavailable) — 0:10–0:20' symptom, must suppress console.warn via the existing vi.spyOn(console, 'warn') pattern, and must use en dash (–, U+2013) inside ranges and em dash (—, U+2014) before them exactly as the source does. Guards AC-4/AC-5/AC-6/AC-7 are already pinned by existing tests (:208-213, :243-258, :215-235, :202-206) and keep passing unmodified. URL parsing itself is untouched per the issue's out_of_scope.\"\n}\n"},"frontier.json":{"sha256":"cda7abf7747634aa5aa1fbeb3383e4e5b02c3d576e4bb24e41a82ea819e7ef10","text":"{\"accepted\":true,\"blockers\":[],\"issue\":49,\"ready\":true,\"ticket_sha256\":\"ab17e76aca296b789fbede992c2f44589eaa3909b2db69b94f73bff047b13ea5\",\"version\":\"1.0\"}\n"},"issue-frontier.json":{"sha256":"06b5215d9448dcf3822fc555f4895b97c2327900c4d8bdabed0c73843c499a18","text":"{\"blockers\":[],\"fetched_at\":\"2026-09-11T11:57:41Z\",\"issue\":{\"body\":\"## Background\\n\\n`formatCitation` in `app/frontend/src/lib/exportMarkdown.ts` renders each citation in an exported conversation. Its YouTube fallback path is wrong: when `citation.video_url`