on its own line, so formatSources output remains a single markdown list and no entry merges into the previous item.\",\"The fallback paths still emit no markdown link: the YouTube fallback contains no '[<title>](' watch/deep-link, and the Dynamous empty-lesson_url fallback contains no ']('.\",\"The console.warn message '[exportMarkdown] Skipping timestamp link — invalid video_url: \\\"<url>\\\"' is emitted unchanged on both YouTube fallback branches (pinned verbatim by an existing test).\",\"Only one production file changes: app/frontend/src/lib/exportMarkdown.ts; test changes are confined to app/frontend/src/lib/exportMarkdown.test.ts.\"],\"issue\":{\"number\":49,\"title\":\"fix(export): markdown export drops the transcript snippet when a citation URL cannot be parsed\"},\"out_of_scope\":[\"Backend, schema, and any new or changed package dependency.\",\"CitationModal.tsx, Message.tsx, ChatArea.tsx, Sidebar.tsx, and any production file other than app/frontend/src/lib/exportMarkdown.ts.\",\"The valid-URL (YouTube '?v=') and valid-lesson_url happy-path return shapes — they are kept as-is and proven by guards AC-4/AC-5, not modified.\",\"formatTimestamp, the export header, and the filename slug.\",\"Changing URL parsing itself (e.g. adding youtu.be/<id> path-ID support): repairing the no-v fallback incidentally improves youtu.be exports, but the parsing logic stays as-is per the issue's scope.\"],\"risks\":[\"REPRO DEFERRED TO RED: no existing command fails on the unchanged tree — the three existing fallback tests were written against the buggy return strings — so the red proof exists only through the new AC-1..AC-3 checkpoints, which must be shown failing (with '(timestamp link unavailable) — 0:10–0:20' in a red checkpoint's output) before the fix is applied.\",\"The exact repaired fallback string is not pinned beyond AC-1/AC-2/AC-3 (marker, '(timestamp link unavailable)' plus range, blockquote on its own line); any shape satisfying them while keeping every current case green is acceptable.\",\"En dash (–, U+2013) inside timestamp ranges vs em dash (—, U+2014) before them are easily swapped in assertions or output; both the fixed code and the new tests must use the same characters as the existing source.\",\"vitest only embeds the received string in toMatch/toContain-style assertion failures; a boolean assertion like expect(result.startsWith('- ')).toBe(true) would go red without displaying the expected symptom, so the AC-1/AC-2 red checkpoints should assert on the result string content.\",\"console.warn must be suppressed (or mocked) in the new tests where it fires, matching the existing suite's vi.spyOn(console, 'warn') pattern, so the checkpoints do not pollute output.\"],\"summary\":\"Repair the three fallback return statements in formatCitation (app/frontend/src/lib/exportMarkdown.ts:32, :46, :53) so every citation entry — the YouTube unparseable-video_url and no-v-param fallbacks and the Dynamous empty-lesson_url fallback — keeps the quoted transcript snippet blockquote and the leading '- ' list marker, matching the shape the valid paths already emit; append AC-1..AC-3 acceptance cases to the existing app/frontend/src/lib/exportMarkdown.test.ts without breaking any current case.\",\"version\":\"2.0\"}\n"},"task-contract.raw.json":{"sha256":"d861ea04d9ba5f06a715091af68022db1fbc557a4ca3f4f0ad51ef783277349a","text":"{\n  \"version\": \"2.0\",\n  \"issue\": {\n    \"number\": 49,\n    \"title\": \"fix(export): markdown export drops the transcript snippet when a citation URL cannot be parsed\"\n  },\n  \"summary\": \"Repair the three fallback return statements in formatCitation (app/frontend/src/lib/exportMarkdown.ts:32, :46, :53) so every citation entry — the YouTube unparseable-video_url and no-v-param fallbacks and the Dynamous empty-lesson_url fallback — keeps the quoted transcript snippet blockquote and the leading '- ' list marker, matching the shape the valid paths already emit; append AC-1..AC-3 acceptance cases to the existing app/frontend/src/lib/exportMarkdown.test.ts without breaking any current case.\",\n  \"behaviors\": [\n    {\n      \"id\": \"AC-1\",\n      \"given\": \"a YouTube citation whose video_url is 'not-a-url' and whose snippet is 'Relevant text' (e.g. { ...baseCitation, video_url: 'not-a-url', snippet: 'Relevant text' } in exportMarkdown.test.ts)\",\n      \"when\": \"formatCitation is called with it\",\n      \"then\": \"the returned string contains the blockquote line '> \\\"Relevant text\\\"' on its own line, in the established two-space-indented shape ('\\\\n  > \\\"<snippet>\\\"') used by every other path. RED proof: on the unchanged tree this assertion fails because the fallback returns only the bare title line, and the failing vitest assertion's received value contains the symptom '(timestamp link unavailable) — 0:10–0:20'\",\n      \"seam\": \"app/frontend/src/lib/exportMarkdown.ts#formatCitation\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"id\": \"AC-2\",\n      \"given\": \"the same citation as AC-1 (video_url 'not-a-url', snippet 'Relevant text')\",\n      \"when\": \"formatCitation is called with it\",\n      \"then\": \"the returned string starts with '- ' and still contains the verbatim substring '(timestamp link unavailable) — 0:10–0:20'. RED proof: on the unchanged tree the string starts with the bare title (no '- ' marker), so the marker assertion fails and the assertion's received value displays '(timestamp link unavailable) — 0:10–0:20'\",\n      \"seam\": \"app/frontend/src/lib/exportMarkdown.ts#formatCitation\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"id\": \"AC-3\",\n      \"given\": \"a citation with source_type 'dynamous' and an empty (or whitespace-only) lesson_url (e.g. { ...baseCitation, source_type: 'dynamous', video_url: '', lesson_url: '' })\",\n      \"when\": \"formatCitation is called with it\",\n      \"then\": \"the returned string starts with '- ', contains no '](' (no markdown link), and still contains its snippet blockquote '> \\\"<snippet>\\\"' (for the existing suite citation, '> \\\"Test snippet text\\\"'). RED proof: on the unchanged tree the string starts with the bare title without '- ', so the marker assertion fails (the blockquote is already present today)\",\n      \"seam\": \"app/frontend/src/lib/exportMarkdown.ts#formatCitation\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"id\": \"AC-4\",\n      \"kind\": \"guard\",\n      \"given\": \"a citation with a valid YouTube video_url carrying a v parameter (the suite's baseCitation: video_url 'https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=abc123', start 10s, end 20s, snippet 'Test snippet text')\",\n      \"when\": \"formatCitation renders it\",\n      \"then\": \"the returned string is unchanged from today's shape (kept behaviour): starts with '- ', contains '[Test Video Title](https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=abc123&t=10s)', the range '0:10–0:20', and the '> \\\"Test snippet text\\\"' blockquote\",\n      \"seam\": \"app/frontend/src/lib/exportMarkdown.ts#formatCitation\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"id\": \"AC-5\",\n      \"kind\": \"guard\",\n      \"given\": \"a citation with source_type 'dynamous' and a non-empty lesson_url (e.g. 'https://community.dynamous.ai/c/module-1/lessons/123')\",\n      \"when\": \"formatCitation renders it\",\n      \"then\": \"the returned string is unchanged from today's shape (kept behaviour): starts with '- ', contains '[Test Video Title](https://community.dynamous.ai/c/module-1/lessons/123)', contains no 'youtube.com' and no '(timestamp link unavailable)', and carries the range and the snippet blockquote\",\n      \"seam\": \"app/frontend/src/lib/exportMarkdown.ts#formatCitation\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"id\": \"AC-6\",\n      \"kind\": \"guard\",\n      \"given\": \"two citations, one whose video_url is unparseable ('not-a-url') and one whose video_url parses but has no v parameter (e.g. 'https://www.youtube.com/')\",\n      \"when\": \"formatCitation renders each\",\n      \"then\": \"each call still emits console.warn with the exact, unchanged message '[exportMarkdown] Skipping timestamp link — invalid video_url: \\\"<video_url>\\\"' (kept behaviour; the message is pinned verbatim by an existing test, so the repair must keep the warn calls)\",\n      \"seam\": \"app/frontend/src/lib/exportMarkdown.ts#formatCitation\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"id\": \"AC-7\",\n      \"kind\": \"guard\",\n      \"given\": \"a citation whose snippet is empty, whitespace-only, or missing\",\n      \"when\": \"formatCitation is called with it\",\n      \"then\": \"the returned string is unchanged from today's shape (kept behaviour): it returns '' via the early guard before any URL handling — no '- ' marker, no blockquote, and no console.warn\",\n      \"seam\": \"app/frontend/src/lib/exportMarkdown.ts#formatCitation\"\n    }\n  ],\n  \"invariants\": [\n    \"Every current case in app/frontend/src/lib/exportMarkdown.test.ts keeps passing; existing cases may be strengthened to pin the repaired fallback shape, but none may be weakened, skipped, or removed.\",\n    \"For any citation with a non-blank snippet, every string formatCitation returns — whatever the source_type or URL validity — starts with '- ' and carries the snippet as a two-space-indented blockquote line ('\\\\n  > \\\"<snippet>\\\"') on its own line, so formatSources output remains a single markdown list and no entry merges into the previous item.\",\n    \"The fallback paths still emit no markdown link: the YouTube fallback contains no '[<title>](' watch/deep-link, and the Dynamous empty-lesson_url fallback contains no ']('.\",\n    \"The console.warn message '[exportMarkdown] Skipping timestamp link — invalid video_url: \\\"<url>\\\"' is emitted unchanged on both YouTube fallback branches (pinned verbatim by an existing test).\",\n    \"Only one production file changes: app/frontend/src/lib/exportMarkdown.ts; test changes are confined to app/frontend/src/lib/exportMarkdown.test.ts.\"\n  ],\n  \"out_of_scope\": [\n    \"Backend, schema, and any new or changed package dependency.\",\n    \"CitationModal.tsx, Message.tsx, ChatArea.tsx, Sidebar.tsx, and any production file other than app/frontend/src/lib/exportMarkdown.ts.\",\n    \"The valid-URL (YouTube '?v=') and valid-lesson_url happy-path return shapes — they are kept as-is and proven by guards AC-4/AC-5, not modified.\",\n    \"formatTimestamp, the export header, and the filename slug.\",\n    \"Changing URL parsing itself (e.g. adding youtu.be/<id> path-ID support): repairing the no-v fallback incidentally improves youtu.be exports, but the parsing logic stays as-is per the issue's scope.\"\n  ],\n  \"risks\": [\n    \"REPRO DEFERRED TO RED: no existing command fails on the unchanged tree — the three existing fallback tests were written against the buggy return strings — so the red proof exists only through the new AC-1..AC-3 checkpoints, which must be shown failing (with '(timestamp link unavailable) — 0:10–0:20' in a red checkpoint's output) before the fix is applied.\",\n    \"The exact repaired fallback string is not pinned beyond AC-1/AC-2/AC-3 (marker, '(timestamp link unavailable)' plus range, blockquote on its own line); any shape satisfying them while keeping every current case green is acceptable.\",\n    \"En dash (–, U+2013) inside timestamp ranges vs em dash (—, U+2014) before them are easily swapped in assertions or output; both the fixed code and the new tests must use the same characters as the existing source.\",\n    \"vitest only embeds the received string in toMatch/toContain-style assertion failures; a boolean assertion like expect(result.startsWith('- ')).toBe(true) would go red without displaying the expected symptom, so the AC-1/AC-2 red checkpoints should assert on the result string content.\",\n    \"console.warn must be suppressed (or mocked) in the new tests where it fires, matching the existing suite's vi.spyOn(console, 'warn') pattern, so the checkpoints do not pollute output.\"\n  ],\n  \"ambiguities\": [],\n  \"dependencies\": []\n}"},"ticket.json":{"sha256":"ab17e